/-! Guidance from the project lead (the requester):

# Guidance: Roquette's idèle computation (Cassels–Fröhlich ch. IX "On class field towers", §3–4)

K/F finite Galois, G a p-group, unramified at all finite primes (different = ⊤) and at infinity (real places
stay real), T a finite set of primes of F that split completely in K, and every p-power ideal class of K lies
in the subgroup generated by the classes of the primes of K above T. Claim:
rank_p Ĥ⁻¹(G, C_K) ≤ r₁ + r₂ − 1 + δ_p(F) + |T|. NO reciprocity law / fundamental class is needed here.

PROOF:
1. Ĥ⁻¹(G, 𝕀_K) = 0 for unramified K/F: 𝕀_K is a restricted product over places of F of the fibres
   ∏_{w|v} K_wˣ ≅ Coind_{D_w}^G K_wˣ (on disk: `NK.GlobalCFTdeep.Herbrand.fiberIdelesRep_iso_coind`); D_w is
   cyclic (unramified) and Ĥ⁻¹(D_w, K_wˣ) ≅ Ĥ¹ = 0 (Hilbert 90 + periodicity); unit parts are cohomologically
   trivial (`hZero_hOne_unitIdelesOutsideRep_eq_one`, `natCard_tateCohomology_fiberUnitsRep_eq_one`,
   `hZero_localUnitSubRep_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one`); use the S-idèles `TIdeles` of `Herbrand/SIdeles.lean` and a
   direct limit / finite-support argument for the restricted product. Infinite places: D_w trivial.
2. From 0 → Kˣ → 𝕀_K → C_K → 0 (Milne Lemma 4.2 exactness is on disk: `milneFourTwoExact_nonempty`,
   `quot_TIdeles_mulEquiv_ideleClassGroup`), Ĥ⁻¹(C_K) ≅ ker(Ĥ⁰(G,Kˣ) → Ĥ⁰(G,𝕀_K)) = (Fˣ ∩ N𝕀_K)/N Kˣ.
   A Tate-cohomology lemma of exactly this shape exists in `Submission/Work/CFT/IdeleClassGroup/
   tateCohomology_minus_one_iso_ker.lean` of the erdos run (copy the argument if useful; it is Mathlib-only).
3. For unramified K_w/F_v, x ∈ F_vˣ is a norm iff f_v | v(x) (`norm_units_surjective_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one`
   in the Commons; local units are norms). Real places: no condition.
4. x ∈ Fˣ ∩ N𝕀_K ⇒ (x) = N_{K/F}(𝔄) for an ideal 𝔄 of K. Let m = order of the prime-to-p part of Cl(K).
   By `hclass`, 𝔄^m = (y)·∏_{w|T} 𝔓_w^{b_w}, and N𝔓_w = 𝔭_v since T splits. So x^m = ε·N(y)·π with ε ∈ E_F and π in
   the group generated by fixed generators of a ℤ-basis of {a ∈ ℤ^T : ∏ 𝔭_v^{a_v} principal} (rank ≤ |T|).
   Ĥ⁻¹ is killed by |G| (a p-power) and gcd(m,p)=1, so x ↦ x^m is bijective on it; hence Ĥ⁻¹ is generated by
   the image of E_F plus ≤ |T| elements, and rank_p ≤ dim_{𝔽_p}(E_F/E_F^p) + |T| = r₁+r₂−1+δ_p + |T|
   (Dirichlet; `NumberField.Units.rank`, torsion = roots of unity).
Delegate each numbered step as its own lemma.
-/

namespace NK.CFTLib

theorem roquette_bound (F K : Type) [Field F] [NumberField F] [Field K] [NumberField K] [Algebra F K]
    [FiniteDimensional F K] [IsGalois F K] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hG : IsPGroup p (K ≃ₐ[F] K))
    (T : Finset (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers F)))
    (hunr : CFTLib.IsUnramified F K) (hT : CFTLib.SplitsAt F K T) (hclass : CFTLib.ClassCond F K p T) :
    Module.finrank (ZMod p)
        (TensorProduct ℤ (ZMod p) (tateCohomology (NK.GlobalCFT.IdeleClassGroup.rep F K) (-1))) ≤
      NumberField.InfinitePlace.nrRealPlaces F + NumberField.InfinitePlace.nrComplexPlaces F - 1 +
        CFTLib.delta F p + T.card := by
  -- Step 1+2: `Ĥ⁻¹(Gal(K/F), C_K)` is the concrete quotient `(Fˣ ∩ N𝕀_K)/N Kˣ`.
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := tateCohomology_neg_one_iso_normQuotient F K hunr
  -- Transport the `𝔽_p`-dimension along the `ℤ`-linear isomorphism.
  refine le_trans (le_of_eq (finrank_tensor_zmod_eq_of_linearEquiv e p)) ?_
  -- Steps 3+4: the rank bound for the concrete quotient.
  exact finrank_normQuotient_le F K p hG T hunr hT hclass

end NK.CFTLib
